  "body": "Part of #894.\n\nThread-milling pass control after #894's first slice is: equal radial passes of at most `infeed`, the last on the thread depth; climb sense assumes a clockwise (M3) spindle and a right-hand cutter.\n\n**What is missing**\n- A spring pass (repeat the final radius) and a finishing-pass depth separate from the roughing step.\n- Decreasing pass depths (constant chip area) as handbooks give for threading.\n- A stated thread depth or diameter allowance (fit adjustment), with a refusal past the standard depth.\n- Left-hand cutters / M4: the climb rule flips with the spindle direction; today the kernel assumes M3.\n- Honouring the operation's `top_z` (R plane) for where the feed starts; the ride reads each hole's own entry.\n\n**Done means:** each control is an operation parameter (file, page, MCP params), gated at command creation, pinned by a kernel test and a golden.\n",
